{"content":"Perfect! I have all the information needed. Let me compile the answer:\n\nq29.\n\n**Interceptor path:** `web/src/connect.ts` (lines 156–178)\n\n**Token kinds managed:**\n1. **Access Token V2** (JWT) – Short-lived (15 minutes), stateless validation via signature\n2. **Refresh Token** (JWT) – Long-lived (30 days), stored in HTTP-only cookie (`memos_refresh`)\n3. **Personal Access Token (PAT)** – Long-lived, programmatic access, prefix `memos_pat_`\n\n**Backend validation package:** `server/auth/authenticator.go` (package `auth`)\n\nThe authentication flow: the frontend's `authInterceptor` in `connect.ts` attaches the access token as a Bearer header (`Authorization: Bearer {token}`). The backend's `AuthInterceptor` (in `server/router/api/v1/connect_interceptors.go` lines 208–230) extracts the header and delegates to the `Authorizer` (in `authz.go`), which calls the `Authenticator` from `server/auth/authenticator.go`. The `Authenticator` validates tokens via three methods: `AuthenticateByAccessTokenV2()` (stateless), `AuthenticateByRefreshToken()` (database revocation check), and `AuthenticateByPAT()` (database lookup).","iteration":11,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
